{
    "background_story": "Daisy was a majestic palomino mare with a shiny coat and a spirited personality. She spent her days galloping through the rolling hills of the countryside, her mane flowing in the wind. But as the seasons passed, Daisy began to feel the effects of age. Her once-luxuriant coat lost its luster, and her joints creaked with a dull ache. Her withers, the highest point of her shoulder, began to sag, a visible sign of her declining strength. Despite this, Daisy's spirit remained unbroken. She continued to run and play, albeit with a more gentle pace, earning the admiration of her owner, a young girl named Sophie. Together, they explored the countryside, Daisy's wisdom and experience guiding Sophie through the ups and downs of life. Even in her twilight years, Daisy remained a proud and noble companion.",
